 "verdict": "Both trips ran on lists \u2014 roughly half of all navigation went to saved places either way (47% self-curated vs 53% source-curated). What changed was content, not discipline: self-curation defaulted to sustenance \u2014 food and coffee dominate Trip 1 \u2014 while sourced guides surfaced the interest profile: books \u00d76.9 (11\u219276), museums & history \u00d72.9 (15\u219244), and record stores from zero in seven cities to 24. Outdoors was flat (14\u219217). Left to itself, curation feeds you; sourced, it takes you somewhere.",
 "disclosure": "Categories are keyword-tagged from the business-name portion of direction requests \u2014 a rough instrument, not hand-curated. Adherence figures are directions-only; list-browsing matches are excluded as circular. Per-item save timestamps don't exist in the export, so pre-trip and in-situ saves can't be perfectly separated."
